            <ArticleTitle>Pain relief in chronic pancreatitis with epidural buprenorphine injection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The management of intractable pain in chronic pancreatitis is difficult. A novel method for its relief is described.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Twelve patients were given a mixture of buprenorphine (0.3 mg) and blood (10-15 mL) into the epidural space.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">All patients had pain relief lasting up to six months.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Epidural buprenorphine injection is a simple, safe and effective method for pain relief in chronic pancreatitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
